---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const Brief = `We had seven applicants and I have their scores. Give me the
ones worth interviewing, best first.`;

const SampleOutput = `4 of 7 scored 75 or better
  1. Ravi (95)
  2. Nadia (88)
  3. Sam (88)
  ...and 1 more above the cutoff

1 of 7 scored 90 or better
  1. Ravi (95)`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp/unit-2/cc-set-6" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back to Set 6
        </a>

        <h1>Code Challenge: Shortlist</h1>

        <h4>
          Difficulty&nbsp;&nbsp;
          <i class="si-star text-sn-green"></i>
          <i class="si-star text-sn-green"></i>
          <i class="si-star text-sn-green"></i>
        </h4>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="brief">
          <h2>The Brief</h2>

          <Code code={Brief} frame="code" lang="txt" title="What they asked for" showLineNumbers={false} class="mt-3" />

          <p class="mt-4">
            <b>Write your requirements list before you write any code.</b> Input,
            calculate, output, and anything you had to decide for yourself. See{" "}
            <a href="/courses/ap-csp/unit-2/cc-set-6">Set 6</a> for what that looks like.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="notes">
          <h2>Notes</h2>

          <ul>
            <li><b>This brief is deliberately underspecified and there is no bonus for guessing what I meant.</b> Write down what it does not tell you, decide, and say so.</li>
            <li>Worth interviewing above what score? How many do you show? What happens if more clear the bar than you are showing?</li>
            <li>There is a tie in any sensible test data. Decide what a tie does before you hit one.</li>
            <li>Run it twice with different settings so you can see the decisions actually take effect.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="sample-output">
          <h2>Sample Output</h2>

          <Code code={SampleOutput} frame="terminal" title="Sample Output" lang="txt" showLineNumbers={false} class="mt-3" />

          <p class="mt-3">
            <b>Nadia and Sam both scored 88.</b> The sample put Nadia first
            because she came first in the original list. That is a decision, not
            an accident, and it belongs in your requirements list.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>
            Your requirements list and your program file, named{" "}
            <b class="text-sn-theme">cc-shortlist</b>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <h1 class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash">
          Commence Challenge
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
